* Functions

A function can take zero or more arguments.

In this example, ⟪GTI18N_accf0562_000001⟫add⟪GTI18N_accf0562_000002⟫ takes two parameters of type ⟪GTI18N_accf0562_000003⟫int⟪GTI18N_accf0562_000004⟫.

Notice that the type comes ⟪GTI18N_accf0562_000005⟫after⟪GTI18N_accf0562_000006⟫ the variable name.

(For more about why types look the way they do, see the [[⟪GTI18N_accf0562_000007⟫][article on ⟪GTI18N_accf0562_000008⟫'s declaration syntax]].)

